{
  "syllabusVersion": "2.0",
  "source": {
    "en": "ISTQB® Certified Tester AI Testing (CT-AI) Syllabus v2.0 (GA 2026-04-17), the per-chapter 'Keywords' and 'AI-Specific Keywords' lists of chapters 1-7",
    "tr": "TTB Certified Tester AI Testing (CT-AI) Syllabus v1.0, Turkish translation (2021): chapter keyword lists ('Anahtar Kelimeler', 'YZ-Spesifik Anahtar Kelimeleri'), the Appendix B term list ('Ek B - Yapay Zekâ Özellikleri ve Diğer Terimler') and body text; plus data/ctfl-v4.0.1/terms.json (TTB CTFL v4.0.1 Turkish syllabus) for general testing terms",
    "method": "Every entry of the v2.0 Keywords and AI-Specific Keywords lists was collected and deduplicated; 'chapters' lists every chapter whose lists name the term. No Turkish v2.0 syllabus exists, so the positional mapping used for CTFL is impossible and each Turkish term was looked up instead. General testing terms reuse data/ctfl-v4.0.1/terms.json exactly, including its trForbidden (trSource 'ttb-syllabus-v4.0.1'). AI terms take the TTB v1.0 Turkish wording, attested as a phrase in the v1.0 keyword lists, Appendix B or body text (trSource 'ttb-ct-ai-v1.0'); where v1.0 uses two words for one term, the one more frequent in the v1.0 text was taken. Terms new in v2.0, and v2.0 compounds not attested as a phrase in v1.0, are editorial translations (trSource 'editorial'), built from the v1.0 or CTFL Turkish words for their parts where those exist."
  },
  "trSource": "mixed",
  "note": "trSource on each term records where its Turkish comes from; 'editorial' terms have no official Turkish source and need review before content relies on them. trForbidden is kept sparse: it lists a rendering found in the TTB v1.0 syllabus only when it would be actively misleading (it names a different concept), plus the trForbidden entries carried over unchanged from the CTFL terms file. 'safety' is 'emniyet', as in this project's CTFL content: the TTB v1.0 syllabus writes 'güvenlik' for both safety and security, and 'güvenlik' stays the word for security. The ML functional performance family uses 'fonksiyonel', which the v1.0 keyword lists and LOs use and which matches CTFL's 'fonksiyonel test'. Added on 02.10.2026 after the first content pass: the terms the writers needed beyond the syllabus keyword lists, settled once so every question and lesson uses the same word. 'precision'/'recall' are the TTB v1.0 'hassasiyet'/'hatırlama' (numeric precision, as in low-precision arithmetic, is 'duyarlık'); the neural-network bias parameter is 'yanlılık değeri', as in TTB v1.0; 'feature engineering' is 'öznitelik mühendisliği', although TTB v1.0 writes 'özellik mühendisliği', because 'özellik' is this product's word for a quality characteristic. The general testing terms defect, failure, error, test case, validation and verification were copied from the CTFL file with their trForbidden lists, so check #21 holds CT-AI content to the same words. A second batch was added on 02.10.2026 after verification: 'agent' is 'ajan' and 'chip' is 'çip', as in TTB v1.0; 'vulnerability' is 'güvenlik açığı', the TTB v1.0 phrase, rather than 'zafiyet'; 'hybrid' is 'hibrit'. 'deterministic' is 'deterministik'; 'belirleyici' is not listed in trForbidden only because it is ordinary Turkish for 'decisive'.",
  "termCount": 156,
